  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a6334982dcae08e4698af5d208c769f4, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question3_Wheatfield
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  description:
  - On the technical side, van Gogh used oil on canvas and applied his paint thickly
    to produce texture. He paired vivid complementary colors, including blue green
    in the sky, yellow orange in the wheat, red in the path, and green in the grass,
    to heighten contrast and emotional tension. His brushwork is energetic and sweeping.
    The sky churns with motion, and the field shows directional strokes that suggest
    wind and disturbance. The composition places the horizon low so that the sky
    dominates almost everything else.
  awnsers:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: c94eb68c7acffcd43b1598730955e457, type: 3}
